op7t-0199: DisplayPipePlaneBaseAlignment as a dictionary (mediaserverd crashed on every video)

2026-11-12: Safari stays black ~20 s on pages with video, and videos never
play. mediaserverd aborts every few seconds:
  -[__NSCFNumber objectForKey:]: unrecognized selector
  ... VideoToolbox FigGetAlignmentForIOSurfaceOutputToDisplayService
  <- MediaToolbox FPSupport_CopyDestinationPixelBufferAttributesWithIOSurfaceSupport
  <- itemfig_createRenderTriplesForVideo (video playback being prepared)
That function (disassembled from the phone's VideoToolbox) reads the display
service's DisplayPipePlaneBaseAlignment and does CFDictionaryGetValue(..,
"PlaneBaseAlignmentLinear") on it (and DisplayPipeStrideRequirements ->
"StrideLinearHorizontal", skipped when absent). 0046 made the first a plain
number 64. Now { PlaneBaseAlignmentLinear = 64 }: same value, the type every
reader in the shared cache expects. DisplayPipeStrideRequirements stays
absent (no change to how surfaces are allocated).

Apply after 0198.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 4b8573d..56e3113 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -340,7 +340,23 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 
 	setProperty(kIOUserClientClassKey, "IOMobileFramebufferUserClient");
 	setProperty("external", false);
-	setProperty("DisplayPipePlaneBaseAlignment", 64ULL, 32);
+	/*
+	 * 0199: a dictionary, as on Apple's AppleCLCD. VideoToolbox's FigGetAlignmentForIOSurfaceOutputToDisplayService
+	 * does CFDictionaryGetValue(DisplayPipePlaneBaseAlignment, "PlaneBaseAlignmentLinear"); the plain number 64 this
+	 * was made it throw "-[__NSCFNumber objectForKey:]", killing mediaserverd every time a video was prepared
+	 * (Safari pages with video, 2026-11-12). The other reader in the shared cache pairs it with the same key.
+	 */
+	{
+		OSDictionary *align = OSDictionary::withCapacity(1);
+		OSNumber *linear = OSNumber::withNumber(64ULL, 32);
+
+		if (align != NULL && linear != NULL) {
+			align->setObject("PlaneBaseAlignmentLinear", linear);
+			setProperty("DisplayPipePlaneBaseAlignment", align);
+		}
+		OSSafeReleaseNULL(linear);
+		OSSafeReleaseNULL(align);
+	}
 	/*
 	 * 0109: present() waits for the GPU's last submission that names a surface before it shows
 	 * it (RedwoodGPUSurfaceReady, both for 0108's flip and the copy), so eagl.c need not glFinish
